# Sky1 (arm64) firmware package set -- the subset of manifests/firmware.pkgs
# that a CIX Sky1 system (Radxa Orion O6N, Minisforums MS-R1 / "cixmini")
# can actually load, plus a deliberately small hotplug allowance.  Selection
# rationale, per-package evidence and restore instructions:
# manifests/firmware-bom-arm64.allow.
#
# manifests/firmware.pkgs stays the complete, architecture-neutral published
# set and is unchanged for amd64 (T2 Macs need brcm/intel/amd).  build/
# build-forky-mirror.sh, build/verify-firmware-bom.sh, build/verify-offline-
# mirror-seeds.sh, build/verify-installed-target.sh and post-install/
# 13-firmware-bom.sh all prefer manifests/firmware-$ARCH.pkgs when it exists,
# so this file is the arm64 install + mirror seed and the arm64 half of the
# closure gate.  The complement (packages deliberately NOT shipped on arm64)
# is manifests/firmware-bom-arm64.allow; verify-firmware-bom.sh fails unless
# published == declared U declared-in-allow for the target arch.
#
# KEEP set:
#   on-board Sky1 SoC /
#   MS-R1 M.2 WiFi+BT:  realtek (RTL8125/8127 rtl_nic, RTW89 Sky1 M.2,
#                       r8152 USB-ETH, rtw88/rtl_bt), mediatek (MT7922/Mt7961/
#                       MT7925 -- MS-R1 M.2 module)
#   hotplug allowance:  atheros (ath9k/ath10k/ath11k/ath12k QCNFA M.2/PCIe and
#                       USB dongles), ath9k-htc (tiny USB), amd-graphics
#                       (amdgpu works on arm64; the O6N has a real PCIe slot)
#   metapackages/deps:  firmware-linux{,-free,-nonfree} (firmware-linux-nonfree
#                       Depends: firmware-misc-nonfree, firmware-amd-graphics)
#   catch-all:          misc-nonfree (dependency of firmware-linux-nonfree;
#                       carries kernel-wide misc blobs)
firmware-amd-graphics
firmware-ath9k-htc
firmware-atheros
firmware-linux
firmware-linux-free
firmware-linux-nonfree
firmware-mediatek
firmware-misc-nonfree
firmware-realtek
